\details{
\code{ggthemes_data$stata$colors$names} spans both generations of Stata's
named colors: the classic set plus the \code{gs0}--\code{gs16} gray scale,
and the \code{stc1}--\code{stc15} colors added in Stata 18. See
\code{\link[=stata_pal]{stata_pal()}}.

Colors, shapes and linetypes are stored with the theme they belong to. The
\href{https://jrnold.github.io/ggthemes/articles/data.html}{Package data}
article on the package website draws every one of them. \code{ggthemes_data}
contains no fonts: themes set their typefaces in code.

\code{ggthemes_data$economist_2017} contains the colors of \emph{The Economist
visual styleguide} (v1.2, 4 May 2017), one complete set per medium
(\code{print} and \code{web}): the ground, gridline, text, baseline, source and
accent colors used by \code{\link[=theme_economist_2017]{theme_economist_2017()}}, the categorical palettes
used by \code{\link[=economist_2017_pal]{economist_2017_pal()}}, and the equal-lightness ramps used by
\code{\link[=economist_2017_gradient_pal]{economist_2017_gradient_pal()}}. The palettes and ramps are the same for
both media. \code{ggthemes_data$economist_2017$print$swatches} lists every
swatch of the guide's print chart palette: its name and group as the guide
gives them, the CMYK it specifies (\code{c}, \code{m}, \code{y}, \code{k}, in percent), and
that CMYK converted to sRGB through ISO Coated v2 (FOGRA39), relative
colorimetric with black-point compensation. The print colors are drawn
from these swatches, except the black text and source text, which convert
their K percentage directly. \code{ggthemes_data$economist_2017$web$swatches}
lists the hex swatches of the guide's web palette page, for reference.

\code{ggthemes_data$economist_design_system} contains the complete color
tokens extracted from the current Economist Design System and Marber
documentation. Numeric HSL is the canonical representation; the published
HEX, RGB, HSL, and (where available) CMYK values are retained as documented
source fields. The object also includes derived five-point HSL ramps for the
main color families. These product tokens are kept separate from the
observed chart palettes in \code{ggthemes_data$economist_2024}.
